The <ansi fg="command">goal</ansi> command inspects and seeds the
strategic-layer goals held by a mob template. Goals drive future
behavior-tree planning (chunk 4.4+); this admin entry point exists
for inspection, smoke-testing, and one-off seeding.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Usage:</ansi>

<ansi fg="command">goal list <mob-ident></ansi>
  List every goal on the mob, sorted priority-desc then id-asc.

<ansi fg="command">goal show <mob-ident> <goal-id></ansi>
  Show one goal's full record (type, priority, params,
  timestamps).

<ansi fg="command">goal add <mob-ident> <type> <priority> [key=value ...]</ansi>
  Append a new goal. Conflicting existing goals with strictly
  lower priority are displaced; equal-or-higher priority blocks
  the Add. key=value params parse as int -> float -> bool ->
  string (no quoting needed).

<ansi fg="command">goal remove <mob-ident> <goal-id></ansi> (alias: <ansi fg="command">rm</ansi>)
  Delete a single goal by id (e.g. <ansi fg="cyan">g3</ansi>).

<ansi fg="command">goal clear <mob-ident></ansi>
  Wipe every goal on the mob and reset the goal-id counter to 1.
  Intentionally heavy-hand — admin-only reset.

<ansi fg="command">goal current <mob-ident></ansi>
  Show the cached selection state for a mob — which goal is current,
  when it became current, and the reason it won the last selection
  cycle. Chunk 4.2.

<ansi fg="command">goal scores <mob-ident></ansi>
  Show the full score breakdown table for a mob: every goal's
  effective score (priority x archetype weight x contextMod), the
  CURRENT marker, and which goals are filtered out. Chunk 4.2.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Mob identifier:</ansi>
  Numeric template id (e.g. <ansi fg="cyan">371</ansi>) or namesimple
  (e.g. <ansi fg="cyan">tova</ansi>, <ansi fg="cyan">stillwater_smith</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Notes:</ansi>
  - Changes persist immediately to
    <ansi fg="cyan">_datafiles/world/dogmud/goals/{mobId}-{namesimple}.yaml</ansi>.
  - Goal ids are short and stable (<ansi fg="cyan">g1</ansi>, <ansi fg="cyan">g2</ansi>, ...) and
    never reuse within a file's lifetime (except via <ansi fg="command">clear</ansi>).
  - The goal-type registry is empty at chunk 4.1 ship; chunk 4.3
    fills it with concrete goal types.
